    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d417">

                <pb facs="0489" n="483" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg483"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/26441: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Henderson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi><anchor n="71" xml:id="d417-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kuibyshev</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-12-11T19:00:00+03:00">December 11, 1942—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 12—9:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1082. Your 620, December 9, 1 [<hi rendition="#italic">6</hi>] p.m., received
                    here this morning. I am leaving for Moscow by earliest available transportation
                    in <pb facs="0490" n="484" xml:id="pg484"/> order to carry out the instructions
                    contained therein and shall probably see Molotov Monday or Tuesday.<anchor
                        n="72" xml:id="d417-f2"/> I would appreciate in the meantime such
                    clarification as the Department may be able to telegraph me at Moscow with
                    regard to the sentence beginning, “This will not be the case.” Molotov is
                    certain to ask me who the “other Frenchmen” are and perhaps in what respect
                    their political aims have “never been ‘gone along with’ by the Government”.
                    Without such clarification I shall not be able to answer these questions and I
                    fear that consequently our conversation may not be fully satisfactory.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henderson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d417-f1" n="71" type="source" xml:id="d417-f1-content">
                <p>A penciled note on this telegram made in the Department reads: “No reply sent
                    since it was felt it would be better not to discuss personalities.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d417-f2" n="72" xml:id="d417-f2-content">
                <p>December 14 or 15. For Henderson’s conversation with Molotov, see his telegram
                    No. 537, December 15, 9 p.m., below.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
